{"t": 1795069641.99141, "kind": "assistant", "text": "## Stopped: PHP 8.3 validation failed\n\n- **Dev snapshot:** `dev/pre-php-8.3-upgrade.tgz`\n- **Dev PHP:** upgraded from 8.1.34 to **8.3.31**\n- **Page checks:**\n  - `/` → **500**, PHP fatal error naming `limit-login-attempts-reloaded`\n  - `/wp-login.php` → **200**\n  - `/wp-admin/` → **200**\n\n`limit-login-attempts-reloaded` 3.4.4 remains active. I did **not** deactivate it or include the requested deactivation command.\n\nBecause the plugin appears incompatible and the front end fails, I stopped as required and **did not submit a production change plan**. Production remains unchanged on PHP 8.1.34. A human should investigate a compatible plugin update or fix and repeat dev validation before considering a production upgrade."}
